RUN 3 CONTROLLER FIXES (on top of the dead runs' WIP):
1. capture harness: shot() passed {} as the CDP sessionId (crash: "Message
   may have string 'sessionId'"); removed the third arg (flatten:true
   session rides send()'s default).
2. capture harness: getComputedStyle(null) crashes when .btn--primary is
   absent on the Progress/Practice routes — guarded, FAILs instead of dying.
3. capture harness: section-5 scroll IIFE had unbalanced parens
   ("Unexpected end of input") — closed.
4. capture harness: primary button was measured at y=-1907 (off-viewport
   after the resume auto-scroll) so the CDP press landed nowhere — added
   scrollIntoView before measuring; press/release now also wait for the
   120ms family transitions to settle (settled state is check 3's claim;
   transition-presence is check 2's claim, unchanged).
5. capture harness: token check compared literal '120ms' but Chrome
   normalizes custom-property times to '.12s' — compare semantically.
6. REAL BUG (App.tsx): the gliding-underline effect keyed on [route] never
   measured the nav after profile resume (chooser renders without routeNav;
   resume mounts the nav with no route change). Now the effect runs per
   render, measures every time (route changes move aria-current on a stable
   nav node), and re-arms the ResizeObserver only when the nav node
   changes.
7. motion-contract.test.ts: ruleBody() whitespace-normalizes so prettier's
   (CI-mandated) declaration wrapping can't break the token assertions;
   assertions unchanged in substance, still RED at base.
8. stale lts-storage rlib (worktree artifact, skill pitfall) made HEAD
   uncompilable ('NewCapstoneAttempt not found'); cargo clean -p
   lts-storage + rebuild fixed it. No source change.

